// 26 U.S.C. §§6673-6702 (IRC-16 STAGE 2, DECISION-0379) — a bounded first
// slice of Chapter 68 Subchapter B "Assessable Penalties" NOT covered by
// stage 1: §6673(a)(1) (Tax Court sanction for frivolous/dilatory
// proceedings), §6674 (fraudulent/willful failure to furnish an employee
// statement, flat $50), §6675 (excessive fuel-credit claims, greater-of
// 2x-or-$10), §6676 (erroneous refund/credit claims, 20 percent), §6682
// (false statement reducing withholding, flat $500, with the (b) waiver
// power and the (c) deficiency-procedure immunity), §6702(a)/(b) (frivolous
// returns and frivolous specified submissions, flat $5,000 each, with the
// (b)(3) 30-day cure).
//
// STAGE-2 SCOPE NOTE (see report): this module is a PARTIAL slice of the
// stage-2 assignment's much larger list (§§6652, 6655, 6662 remainder, 6663
// remainder, 6664(d), 6665 remainder, 6672, 6677, 6679, 6684-6701 (other than
// 6682/6694/6695/6698 fragments not attempted here), 6704-6725, 6751(b)(2),
// 6801-6873 are NOT touched by this change — they remain `unreviewed`
// pending further stage-2 work). This module was chosen because each of its
// provisions is a single-ground, non-cross-referencing flat or two-term
// penalty that fits the package's existing calculation-relation pattern
// (05-failure-to-deposit-6656.law, 06-definitions-and-fraud-6663-6664.law)
// without a new dependency contract.
//
// JUDGMENT CALLS AND GAPS (see report):
//  - §6673(a)(1) is DISCRETIONARY ("the Tax Court ... MAY require ... a
//    penalty NOT IN EXCESS OF $25,000"): this module models the three
//    triggering conditions and the $25,000 cap as a `power` of the Tax
//    Court (matching E-0239's invalid-exercise discipline for a power whose
//    exercise is optional even when valid), but the EXACT dollar amount
//    within the cap is the Tax Court's own discretionary determination — an
//    empirical fact of the proceeding's record (`tax_court_sanction_amount`),
//    range-restricted only by the cap, not itself computed. §6673(a)(2)
//    (counsel's liability for excessive costs — a fee-shifting rule between
//    the attorney/United States, not a taxpayer penalty) is NOT modelled —
//    TECH_GAP (see TECH-GAPS.md).
//  - §6674's "willfully" (both the false-statement and the failure-to-furnish
//    branches) is a DECISION-0194 evaluative element: this module reuses the
//    package's existing `reasonable_cause_and_no_willful_neglect`-style
//    pattern only where the statute's own text supports it; here the statute
//    itself makes willfulness an ELEMENT of liability (not an affirmative
//    defense to an otherwise-strict rule), so it is modelled as a plain
//    empirical predicate the case must assert (`willfully_furnished_false_
//    employee_statement` / `willfully_failed_to_furnish_employee_statement`),
//    consistent with how E-0239's authors treat willfulness-as-element versus
//    willfulness-as-rebuttal (see 06-definitions-and-fraud-6663-6664.law's
//    fraud module for the rebuttal pattern).
//  - §6675(a)'s and §6676(a)'s "reasonable cause" is a NEW, THIRD evaluative
//    channel (`reasonable_cause_for_excessive_claim`), textually distinct
//    from both the §6651/6654 "reasonable cause and not due to willful
//    neglect" standard and the §6664(c) "reasonable cause ... and good
//    faith" standard (01-shared.law / 06-definitions-and-fraud module's own
//    documented reasoning for keeping textually distinct standards apart).
//  - §6676(c)'s carve-out (an excessive amount attributable to a section
//    6662(b)(6) economic-substance transaction is NEVER reasonable cause) is
//    modelled as a defeater on the reasonable-cause exception itself, not a
//    separate rate.
//  - §6676(d) (coordination — this section does not apply to any portion
//    already subject to a Chapter 68 Part II fraud/accuracy penalty) and
//    §6675(c) (assessment/collection cross-reference to §6206) and §6702(f)
//    (partnership adjustment requests treated as returns) are NON_NORMATIVE
//    cross-references for this module's purposes — no independent norm to
//    execute, each is a pointer to a rule owned elsewhere (or, for 6702(f),
//    a scope extension this package does not need for the (a)/(b) core).
//  - §6682(a)'s "statement under section 3402 or 3406" is a NEW LOCAL entity
//    (`WithholdingStatement`): neither section 3402 (wage withholding) nor
//    3406 (backup withholding) machinery is modelled in this package
//    (`employment`, F-series, is a different owner), so the statement is
//    reified locally with only the empirical facts §6682 itself needs
//    (who made it, whether it decreased withholding, whether there was a
//    reasonable basis) — EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY-adjacent for the underlying
//    withholding computation, not for the penalty itself.
//  - §6682(b)'s waiver is modelled as a `power` of the Secretary (matches
//    §6656(c)/(d)'s waiver/abatement pattern in this same package).
//  - §6682(c)'s "deficiency procedures ... shall not apply" is modelled as
//    an `immunity` (protected effect: the ordinary deficiency-notice power
//    of `us.irc.assessment` — a pending package, EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY — does
//    not reach this penalty). Because `assessment` is not yet a declared
//    dependency of this package (stage-1 chose typed contracts, not real
//    imports, per AGENT-BRIEF), the immunity's `protected_effect` targets a
//    LOCAL placeholder relation (`deficiency_procedure_would_apply`) with a
//    coverage-row/deps.json row recording the real cross-package target.
//  - §6702(a)'s "position which the Secretary has identified as frivolous
//    under subsection (c)" and (c) itself (the Secretary's published list)
//    are a case-asserted empirical fact
//    (`position_identified_as_frivolous_under_6702c`), not a derivation of
//    which positions ARE frivolous — publishing and maintaining that list
//    is an institutional act with no further statutory test in the text
//    pinned to this package (classification EXECUTABLE for the fact's USE,
//    NON_NORMATIVE for (c)'s duty to publish, since nothing computable
//    follows from "shall prescribe (and periodically revise) a list").
//  - §6702(d) (discretionary reduction) is modelled as a `power` of the
//    Secretary to reduce; the exact reduced amount is the Secretary's own
//    discretionary determination, same pattern as §6673(a)(1)'s cap.
//  - §6702(e) (penalties under this section are IN ADDITION to any other
//    penalty) is NON_NORMATIVE: it forecloses an implicit-exclusivity
//    reading but states no independent computable rule.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irc.penalties version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irc:penalties:clir";

use self::{
    Claim,
    IRC_S6673_A,
    IRC_S6674,
    IRC_S6675_A,
    IRC_S6675_B,
    IRC_S6676_A,
    IRC_S6676_B,
    IRC_S6682_A,
    IRC_S6682_B,
    IRC_S6682_C,
    IRC_S6702_A,
    IRC_S6702_B,
    IRC_S6702_D,
    Person,
    Return,
    Secretary,
    TaxCourt,
    TaxKind,
    TaxableYear,
};

// =============================================================================
// §6673(a)(1) — Tax Court sanction for frivolous or dilatory proceedings
// =============================================================================

pub entity TaxCourtProceeding {
    label en unofficial "a proceeding before the Tax Court instituted or maintained by a taxpayer";
}
relation tax_court_proceeding_of(proc: TaxCourtProceeding, p: Person) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "the taxpayer who instituted or maintains the proceeding";
}
relation instituted_or_maintained_primarily_for_delay(proc: TaxCourtProceeding) kind empirical {
    label en official "proceedings before it have been instituted or maintained by the taxpayer primarily for delay";
}
relation position_frivolous_or_groundless(proc: TaxCourtProceeding) kind empirical {
    label en official "the taxpayer's position in such proceeding is frivolous or groundless";
}
relation unreasonably_failed_to_pursue_administrative_remedies(proc: TaxCourtProceeding) kind empirical {
    label en official "the taxpayer unreasonably failed to pursue available administrative remedies";
}

pub relation frivolous_proceeding_sanction_conditions_met(proc: TaxCourtProceeding) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "one of the section 6673(a)(1)(A)-(C) grounds for a Tax Court sanction appears to the Tax Court (single atom for the power's valid_when, per the pilot's lesson — LDC-E1305/E0201/E4101)";
}
@source(IRC_S6673_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "proceedings before it have been instituted or maintained by the taxpayer primarily for delay")
rule FrivolousProceedingGroundDelay strict {
    for proc: TaxCourtProceeding;
    when instituted_or_maintained_primarily_for_delay(proc);
    then frivolous_proceeding_sanction_conditions_met(proc);
}
@source(IRC_S6673_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "the taxpayer's position in such proceeding is frivolous or groundless")
rule FrivolousProceedingGroundPosition strict {
    for proc: TaxCourtProceeding;
    when position_frivolous_or_groundless(proc);
    then frivolous_proceeding_sanction_conditions_met(proc);
}
@source(IRC_S6673_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "the taxpayer unreasonably failed to pursue available administrative remedies")
rule FrivolousProceedingGroundRemedies strict {
    for proc: TaxCourtProceeding;
    when unreasonably_failed_to_pursue_administrative_remedies(proc);
    then frivolous_proceeding_sanction_conditions_met(proc);
}

pub relation tax_court_sanction_authorized(proc: TaxCourtProceeding) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "the Tax Court may, in its decision, require the taxpayer to pay a section 6673(a)(1) penalty (up to the cap; the exact amount is the Tax Court's own discretionary determination, not computed here)";
}
relation tax_court_moves_to_sanction(proc: TaxCourtProceeding) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the Tax Court's decision requires the taxpayer to pay a section 6673(a)(1) penalty (the exercise fact of the power)";
}
@source(IRC_S6673_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "the Tax Court, in its decision, may require the taxpayer to pay to the United States a penalty not in excess of $25,000")
rule Section6673a1SanctionPower(proc: TaxCourtProceeding) strict {
    label en official "the Tax Court, in its decision, may require the taxpayer to pay to the United States a penalty not in excess of $25,000";
    when tax_court_moves_to_sanction(proc);
    then power TaxCourtImposeFrivolousProceedingSanction {
        holder TaxCourt;
        over proc;
        exercise tax_court_moves_to_sanction(proc);
        valid_when frivolous_proceeding_sanction_conditions_met(proc);
        effect create(tax_court_sanction_authorized(proc));
        window [@1990-01-01, infinity);
    };
}
relation tax_court_sanction_amount(proc: TaxCourtProceeding, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the amount the Tax Court's decision actually requires the taxpayer to pay under section 6673(a)(1) (a case fact bounded by the cap, not computed by this package — the discretionary point within the range is the Tax Court's own act)";
}
pub relation tax_court_sanction_within_cap(proc: TaxCourtProceeding) kind institutional {
    label en official "a penalty not in excess of $25,000";
}
@source(IRC_S6673_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "a penalty not in excess of $25,000")
rule Section6673a1SanctionWithinCap strict {
    for proc: TaxCourtProceeding;
    for amount: Money;
    when tax_court_sanction_authorized(proc)
        and tax_court_sanction_amount(proc, amount)
        and amount <= round(TaxCourtFrivolousProceedingSanctionCap, 2, "HALF_UP");
    then tax_court_sanction_within_cap(proc);
}

// =============================================================================
// §6674 — Fraudulent statement or failure to furnish statement to employee
// =============================================================================

pub entity EmployeeStatement {
    label en unofficial "a statement required under section 6051 or 6053(b) to be furnished to an employee (e.g. Form W-2 or a tip-income statement)";
}
relation employee_statement_required_of(s: EmployeeStatement, p: Person) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "PENDING-adjacent (owner of sections 6051/6053(b) requirement detail: employment, F-series) — the person required to furnish this statement";
}
relation willfully_furnished_false_employee_statement(s: EmployeeStatement) kind empirical {
    label en official "willfully furnishes a false or fraudulent statement";
}
relation willfully_failed_to_furnish_employee_statement(s: EmployeeStatement) kind empirical {
    label en official "willfully fails to furnish a statement in the manner, at the time, and showing the information required under section 6051 or 6053(b), or regulations prescribed thereunder";
}

pub relation fraudulent_employee_statement_penalty(s: EmployeeStatement, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "shall for each such failure be subject to a penalty under this subchapter of $50";
}
@source(IRC_S6674, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "who willfully furnishes a false or fraudulent statement, or who willfully fails to furnish a statement in the manner, at the time, and showing the information required under section 6051 or 6053(b)")
rule Section6674PenaltyFalseStatement strict {
    for s: EmployeeStatement;
    when willfully_furnished_false_employee_statement(s);
    then fraudulent_employee_statement_penalty(s, round(FraudulentEmployeeStatementPenaltyAmount, 2, "HALF_UP"));
}
@source(IRC_S6674, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "who willfully fails to furnish a statement in the manner, at the time, and showing the information required under section 6051 or 6053(b)")
rule Section6674PenaltyFailureToFurnish strict {
    for s: EmployeeStatement;
    when willfully_failed_to_furnish_employee_statement(s);
    then fraudulent_employee_statement_penalty(s, round(FraudulentEmployeeStatementPenaltyAmount, 2, "HALF_UP"));
}

// =============================================================================
// §6675 — Excessive claims with respect to the use of certain fuels
// =============================================================================

relation fuel_credit_claim_amount(c: Claim, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the amount claimed under section 6416(a)(4), 6420, 6421, or 6427 for a period";
}
relation fuel_credit_allowable_amount(c: Claim, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "PENDING (owner of sections 6416/6420/6421/6427 computation) — the amount allowable under the applicable section for the period";
}
pub relation fuel_credit_excessive_amount(c: Claim, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the term \"excessive amount\" means in the case of any person the amount by which the amount claimed ... exceeds ... the amount allowable";
}
@source(IRC_S6675_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "the amount claimed under section 6416(a)(4), 6420, 6421, or 6427, as the case may be, for any period, exceeds")
rule FuelCreditExcessiveAmount strict {
    for c: Claim;
    for claimed: Money;
    for allowable: Money;
    when fuel_credit_claim_amount(c, claimed) and fuel_credit_allowable_amount(c, allowable);
    then fuel_credit_excessive_amount(c, max(0.00 USD, claimed - allowable));
}

pub external judgment relation reasonable_cause_for_excessive_claim(p: Person, c: Claim) {
    authority Secretary;
    label en official "it is shown that the claim for such excessive amount is due to reasonable cause";
}

pub relation excessive_fuel_claim_penalty(c: Claim, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the person making such claim shall be liable to a penalty in an amount equal to whichever of the following is the greater: (1) Two times the excessive amount; or (2) $10";
}
@source(IRC_S6675_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "the person making such claim shall be liable to a penalty in an amount equal to whichever of the following is the greater")
rule Section6675Penalty defeasible {
    for c: Claim;
    for p: Person;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for kind: TaxKind;
    for camt: Money;
    for excess: Money;
    when us.irc.core::claim_of(c, p, y, kind, camt)
        and fuel_credit_excessive_amount(c, excess);
    then excessive_fuel_claim_penalty(c,
        max(round(excess * ExcessiveFuelClaimMultiplier, 2, "HALF_UP"), round(ExcessiveFuelClaimMinimum, 2, "HALF_UP")));
    unless reasonable_cause_for_excessive_claim(p, c)
        and us.irc.core::claim_of(c, p, y, kind, camt)
        and fuel_credit_excessive_amount(c, excess);
}

// =============================================================================
// §6676 — Erroneous claim for refund or credit
// =============================================================================

relation refund_claim_amount(c: Claim, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the amount of the claim for refund or credit with respect to income tax for the taxable year";
}
relation refund_claim_allowable_amount(c: Claim, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "PENDING (owner: the substantive credit/refund provision claimed under) — the amount of such claim allowable under this title for the taxable year";
}
pub relation refund_claim_excessive_amount(c: Claim, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the term \"excessive amount\" means ... the amount by which the amount of the claim for refund or credit for any taxable year exceeds the amount of such claim allowable under this title for such taxable year";
}
@source(IRC_S6676_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "the amount by which the amount of the claim for refund or credit for any taxable year exceeds the amount of such claim allowable under this title for such taxable year")
rule RefundClaimExcessiveAmount strict {
    for c: Claim;
    for claimed: Money;
    for allowable: Money;
    when refund_claim_amount(c, claimed) and refund_claim_allowable_amount(c, allowable);
    then refund_claim_excessive_amount(c, max(0.00 USD, claimed - allowable));
}

relation excessive_amount_attributable_to_economic_substance_transaction(c: Claim) kind empirical {
    label en official "any excessive amount which is attributable to any transaction described in section 6662(b)(6)";
}
relation excessive_amount_subject_to_part_ii_penalty(c: Claim) kind empirical {
    label en official "any portion of the excessive amount of a claim for refund or credit which is subject to a penalty imposed under part II of subchapter A of chapter 68 (i.e. accuracy-related or fraud)";
}

pub relation erroneous_refund_claim_penalty(c: Claim, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the person making such claim shall be liable for a penalty in an amount equal to 20 percent of the excessive amount";
}
@source(IRC_S6676_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "the person making such claim shall be liable for a penalty in an amount equal to 20 percent of the excessive amount")
rule Section6676Penalty defeasible {
    for c: Claim;
    for p: Person;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for camt: Money;
    for excess: Money;
    when us.irc.core::claim_of(c, p, y, us.irc.core::IncomeCh1, camt)
        and refund_claim_excessive_amount(c, excess)
        and not excessive_amount_subject_to_part_ii_penalty(c);
    then erroneous_refund_claim_penalty(c, round(excess * ErroneousRefundClaimRate, 2, "HALF_UP"));
    unless reasonable_cause_for_excessive_claim(p, c)
        and not excessive_amount_attributable_to_economic_substance_transaction(c)
        and us.irc.core::claim_of(c, p, y, us.irc.core::IncomeCh1, camt)
        and refund_claim_excessive_amount(c, excess)
        and not excessive_amount_subject_to_part_ii_penalty(c);
}

// =============================================================================
// §6682 — False information with respect to withholding
// =============================================================================

pub entity WithholdingStatement {
    label en unofficial "a statement made by an individual under section 3402 or section 3406 (local reification — the underlying withholding computation is EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY, owner: employment)";
}
relation withholding_statement_by(s: WithholdingStatement, p: Person) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "the individual who made the statement";
}
relation results_in_decreased_withholding(s: WithholdingStatement) kind empirical {
    label en official "results in a decrease in the amounts deducted and withheld under chapter 24";
}
relation no_reasonable_basis_for_statement(s: WithholdingStatement) kind empirical {
    label en official "as of the time such statement was made, there was no reasonable basis for such statement";
}

pub relation false_withholding_statement_penalty(s: WithholdingStatement, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "such individual shall pay a penalty of $500 for such statement";
}
@source(IRC_S6682_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "such individual shall pay a penalty of $500 for such statement")
rule Section6682Penalty strict {
    for s: WithholdingStatement;
    when results_in_decreased_withholding(s) and no_reasonable_basis_for_statement(s);
    then false_withholding_statement_penalty(s, round(FalseWithholdingStatementPenaltyAmount, 2, "HALF_UP"));
}

// (b): Secretary's waiver power.
relation withholding_penalty_waiver_condition_met(s: WithholdingStatement, p: Person) kind institutional {
    label en official "the taxes imposed with respect to the individual under subtitle A for the taxable year are equal to or less than the sum of the credits ... and the payments of estimated tax";
}
relation subtitle_a_tax_liability(p: Person, y: TaxableYear, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "PENDING (owner: income-individual) — the taxes imposed on the individual under subtitle A for the taxable year";
}
relation part_iv_chapter_1_credits(p: Person, y: TaxableYear, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "PENDING (owner: income-individual) — credits against subtitle A tax allowed by part IV of subchapter A of chapter 1";
}
relation estimated_tax_payments_considered_paid(p: Person, y: TaxableYear, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "PENDING (owner: payment-refunds-interest) — payments of estimated tax considered payments on account of the subtitle A tax";
}
@source(IRC_S6682_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "the taxes imposed with respect to the individual under subtitle A for the taxable year are equal to or less than the sum of")
rule Section6682bWaiverConditionMet strict {
    for s: WithholdingStatement;
    for p: Person;
    for y: TaxableYear;
    for tax: Money;
    for credits: Money;
    for est: Money;
    when withholding_statement_by(s, p)
        and subtitle_a_tax_liability(p, y, tax)
        and part_iv_chapter_1_credits(p, y, credits)
        and estimated_tax_payments_considered_paid(p, y, est)
        and tax <= credits + est;
    then withholding_penalty_waiver_condition_met(s, p);
}
pub relation false_withholding_statement_penalty_waived(s: WithholdingStatement) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "the section 6682(a) penalty has been waived, in whole or in part, under section 6682(b)";
}
relation secretary_moves_to_waive_withholding_penalty(s: WithholdingStatement) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the Secretary has moved to waive the section 6682(a) penalty (the exercise fact of the (b) power)";
}
@source(IRC_S6682_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "The Secretary may waive (in whole or in part) the penalty imposed under subsection (a)")
rule Section6682bWaiverPower strict {
    label en official "The Secretary may waive (in whole or in part) the penalty imposed under subsection (a) if ...";
    for s: WithholdingStatement;
    for p: Person;
    when secretary_moves_to_waive_withholding_penalty(s)
        and withholding_statement_by(s, p);
    then power WaiveFalseWithholdingStatementPenalty {
        holder Secretary;
        over s;
        exercise secretary_moves_to_waive_withholding_penalty(s);
        valid_when withholding_penalty_waiver_condition_met(s, p);
        effect create(false_withholding_statement_penalty_waived(s));
        window [@1954-08-16, infinity);
    };
}

// (c): deficiency procedures do not apply — modelled as an immunity against
// the (pending, EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY) deficiency-notice power of `assessment`.
relation deficiency_procedure_would_apply(s: WithholdingStatement) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "PENDING (owner: assessment, F02) — placeholder for subchapter B of chapter 63's deficiency procedure reaching this penalty absent the immunity below; see coverage/penalties.deps.json";
}
pub relation false_withholding_statement_penalty_not_subject_to_deficiency_procedure(s: WithholdingStatement) kind institutional {
    label en official "Subchapter B of chapter 63 (relating to deficiency procedures ...) shall not apply in respect to the assessment or collection of any penalty imposed by subsection (a)";
    protected_effect deficiency_procedure_would_apply;
}
@source(IRC_S6682_C, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "Subchapter B of chapter 63 (relating to deficiency procedures for income, estate, gift, and certain excise taxes) shall not apply in respect to the assessment or collection of any penalty imposed by subsection (a)")
rule Section6682cImmunity strict {
    for s: WithholdingStatement;
    for p: Person;
    for amt: Money;
    when false_withholding_statement_penalty(s, amt)
        and withholding_statement_by(s, p);
    then immunity DeficiencyProcedureImmunityFor6682 {
        holder p;
        protected_effect deficiency_procedure_would_apply(s);
        window [@1954-08-16, infinity);
    };
}

// =============================================================================
// §6702(a)/(b) — Frivolous tax returns and frivolous specified submissions
// =============================================================================

relation purported_return_lacks_self_assessment_information(r: Return) kind empirical {
    label en official "does not contain information on which the substantial correctness of the self-assessment may be judged";
}
relation purported_return_facially_substantially_incorrect(r: Return) kind empirical {
    label en official "contains information that on its face indicates that the self-assessment is substantially incorrect";
}
relation position_identified_as_frivolous_under_6702c(r: Return) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the conduct is based on a position which the Secretary has identified as frivolous under section 6702(c) (a case-asserted fact: whether the position appears on the Secretary's published list)";
}
relation reflects_desire_to_delay_or_impede(r: Return) kind empirical {
    label en official "reflects a desire to delay or impede the administration of Federal tax laws";
}

pub relation frivolous_return_form_defect(r: Return) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "section 6702(a)(1): the purported return has either defect named in (a)(1)(A)/(a)(1)(B)";
}
@source(IRC_S6702_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "does not contain information on which the substantial correctness of the self-assessment may be judged")
rule FrivolousReturnFormDefectA strict {
    for r: Return;
    when purported_return_lacks_self_assessment_information(r);
    then frivolous_return_form_defect(r);
}
@source(IRC_S6702_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "contains information that on its face indicates that the self-assessment is substantially incorrect")
rule FrivolousReturnFormDefectB strict {
    for r: Return;
    when purported_return_facially_substantially_incorrect(r);
    then frivolous_return_form_defect(r);
}
pub relation frivolous_return_motive(r: Return) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "section 6702(a)(2): the (a)(1) conduct is based on a frivolous position or reflects a delay/impede motive";
}
@source(IRC_S6702_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "is based on a position which the Secretary has identified as frivolous under subsection (c)")
rule FrivolousReturnMotiveFrivolousPosition strict {
    for r: Return;
    when position_identified_as_frivolous_under_6702c(r);
    then frivolous_return_motive(r);
}
@source(IRC_S6702_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "reflects a desire to delay or impede the administration of Federal tax laws")
rule FrivolousReturnMotiveDelay strict {
    for r: Return;
    when reflects_desire_to_delay_or_impede(r);
    then frivolous_return_motive(r);
}
pub relation frivolous_return_penalty(r: Return, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "A person shall pay a penalty of $5,000 if [the (1) form defect and (2) motive elements are both present]";
}
@source(IRC_S6702_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "A person shall pay a penalty of $5,000 if")
rule Section6702aPenalty strict {
    for r: Return;
    when frivolous_return_form_defect(r) and frivolous_return_motive(r);
    then frivolous_return_penalty(r, round(FrivolousReturnPenaltyAmount, 2, "HALF_UP"));
}

pub entity SpecifiedSubmission {
    label en official "a request for a hearing under section 6320 or 6330, or an application under section 6159, 7122, or 7811";
}
relation specified_submission_of(sub: SpecifiedSubmission, p: Person) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "the person who made the specified submission";
}
relation specified_submission_position_frivolous(sub: SpecifiedSubmission) kind empirical {
    label en official "any portion of such submission is based on a position which the Secretary has identified as frivolous under subsection (c)";
}
relation specified_submission_reflects_desire_to_delay_or_impede(sub: SpecifiedSubmission) kind empirical {
    label en official "reflects a desire to delay or impede the administration of Federal tax laws";
}
pub relation specified_frivolous_submission(sub: SpecifiedSubmission) kind institutional {
    label en official "the term \"specified frivolous submission\" means a specified submission if any portion of such submission is based on a position which the Secretary has identified as frivolous under subsection (c), or reflects a desire to delay or impede the administration of Federal tax laws";
}
@source(IRC_S6702_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "is based on a position which the Secretary has identified as frivolous under subsection (c)")
rule SpecifiedFrivolousSubmissionByPosition strict {
    for sub: SpecifiedSubmission;
    when specified_submission_position_frivolous(sub);
    then specified_frivolous_submission(sub);
}
@source(IRC_S6702_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "reflects a desire to delay or impede the administration of Federal tax laws")
rule SpecifiedFrivolousSubmissionByDelay strict {
    for sub: SpecifiedSubmission;
    when specified_submission_reflects_desire_to_delay_or_impede(sub);
    then specified_frivolous_submission(sub);
}

relation withdrawn_within_30_days_of_notice(sub: SpecifiedSubmission) kind empirical {
    label en official "such person withdraws such submission within 30 days after such notice";
}
pub relation specified_frivolous_submission_penalty(sub: SpecifiedSubmission, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "any person who submits a specified frivolous submission shall pay a penalty of $5,000";
}
@source(IRC_S6702_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "any person who submits a specified frivolous submission shall pay a penalty of $5,000")
rule Section6702bPenalty defeasible {
    for sub: SpecifiedSubmission;
    when specified_frivolous_submission(sub);
    then specified_frivolous_submission_penalty(sub, round(FrivolousSubmissionPenaltyAmount, 2, "HALF_UP"));
    unless withdrawn_within_30_days_of_notice(sub) and specified_frivolous_submission(sub);
}

// (c)/(d)/(e): the Secretary's list-publication duty, the discretionary
// reduction power, and the non-exclusivity statement. Publication (c) is
// NON_NORMATIVE for this package (no computable test follows from "shall
// prescribe (and periodically revise) a list"); (d)'s reduction and (e)'s
// non-exclusivity are recorded below.
relation secretary_moves_to_reduce_6702_penalty(r: Return) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the Secretary has moved to reduce a section 6702 penalty (the exercise fact of the (d) power)";
}
relation reduction_would_promote_compliance(r: Return) kind institutional {
    label en official "the Secretary determines that such reduction would promote compliance with and administration of the Federal tax laws";
}
pub relation section_6702_penalty_reduced(r: Return) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "the amount of a section 6702 penalty on this return has been reduced under section 6702(d) (the exact reduced amount is the Secretary's own discretionary determination, not computed here)";
}
@source(IRC_S6702_D, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "The Secretary may reduce the amount of any penalty imposed under this section if the Secretary determines that such reduction would promote compliance with and administration of the Federal tax laws")
rule Section6702dReductionPower(r: Return) strict {
    label en official "The Secretary may reduce the amount of any penalty imposed under this section if the Secretary determines that such reduction would promote compliance with and administration of the Federal tax laws.";
    when secretary_moves_to_reduce_6702_penalty(r);
    then power ReduceSection6702Penalty {
        holder Secretary;
        over r;
        exercise secretary_moves_to_reduce_6702_penalty(r);
        valid_when reduction_would_promote_compliance(r);
        effect create(section_6702_penalty_reduced(r));
        window [@1982-09-03, infinity);
    };
}
